{
  "id": "Lyo.Authentication.Okta",
  "name": "Lyo.Authentication.Okta",
  "area": "Security",
  "tagline": "Okta SAML profile. The metadata URL uses the public exk key. Request signing and assertion encryption stay off.",
  "description": "Okta SAML profile for `Lyo.Authentication.Saml`. Provider name `okta`, configuration section `OktaAuth`. This profile does not register an OpenID Connect client.",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddOktaProvider(o =>\n{\n    o.Domain = \"lyo.okta.com\";\n    o.AppId = \"exk123\";\n    o.EntityId = \"https://api.example.com/saml\";\n    o.AcsUrl = \"https://api.example.com/auth/callback/okta\";\n});"
    },
    {
      "title": "OktaAuth",
      "language": "json",
      "code": "{\n  \"OktaAuth\": {\n    \"Domain\": \"lyo.okta.com\",\n    \"AppId\": \"exk123\",\n    \"EntityId\": \"https://api.example.com/saml\",\n    \"AcsUrl\": \"https://api.example.com/auth/callback/okta\",\n    \"EmailAttributeName\": \"email\"\n  }\n}"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "list",
      "title": "Metadata and subject",
      "items": [
        "`Domain` is a host (`{org}.okta.com`, `{org}.oktapreview.com`, or a custom domain) with no scheme and no path.",
        "`AppId` is the public `exk…` key from View IdP metadata, not the `0oa…` application id. The metadata URL is `https://{domain}/app/{appId}/sso/saml/metadata`.",
        "The subject is the Okta user id (`00u…`), configured as the NameID or as a `user.id` attribute (`SubjectAttributeName`). The email attribute defaults to `email`.",
        "In the Okta app, the Audience / IdP Identifier must match `EntityId` and the Single sign-on URL must match `AcsUrl`. Leave Signed requests off and assertion encryption off."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "links": [],
